WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:13.602 --> 00:00:18.685
I was born in 1993
in the northern part of North Korea,

00:00:18.709 --> 00:00:21.196
in a town called Hyesan,

00:00:21.220 --> 00:00:23.931
which is on the border with China.

00:00:24.949 --> 00:00:27.479
I had loving parents

00:00:27.503 --> 00:00:29.756
and one older sister.

00:00:31.237 --> 00:00:33.678
Before I was even 10 years old,

00:00:34.516 --> 00:00:37.046
my father was sent to a labor camp

00:00:37.070 --> 00:00:40.281
for engaging in illegal trading.

00:00:41.042 --> 00:00:43.876
Now, by "illegal trading" --

00:00:45.686 --> 00:00:51.903
he was selling clogs, sugar,
rice and later copper

00:00:51.927 --> 00:00:53.339
to feed us.

00:00:55.100 --> 00:01:01.658
In 2007, my sister and I
decided to escape.

00:01:01.682 --> 00:01:04.595
She was 16 years old,

00:01:04.619 --> 00:01:07.269
and I was 13 years old.

00:01:08.809 --> 00:01:13.916
I need you to understand
what the word "escape" means

00:01:13.940 --> 00:01:16.675
in the context of North Korea.

00:01:17.694 --> 00:01:20.021
We were all starving,

00:01:20.045 --> 00:01:24.550
and hunger means death in North Korea.

00:01:25.666 --> 00:01:28.653
So it was the only option for us.

00:01:29.673 --> 00:01:33.850
I didn't even understand
the concept of escape,

00:01:33.874 --> 00:01:37.317
but I could see the lights
from China at night,

00:01:38.486 --> 00:01:43.222
and I wondered if I go where the light is,

00:01:43.246 --> 00:01:46.868
I might be able to find a bowl of rice.

00:01:48.702 --> 00:01:52.340
It's not like we had a grand plan or maps.

00:01:52.364 --> 00:01:55.855
We did not know anything
about what was going to happen.

00:01:57.052 --> 00:02:00.096
Imagine your apartment
building caught fire.

00:02:00.741 --> 00:02:02.843
I mean, what would you do?

00:02:02.867 --> 00:02:05.449
Would you stay there to be burned,

00:02:05.473 --> 00:02:07.843
or would you jump off out of the window

00:02:07.867 --> 00:02:09.451
and see what happens?

00:02:09.966 --> 00:02:11.398
That's what we did.

00:02:11.422 --> 00:02:14.280
We jumped out of the house

00:02:14.304 --> 00:02:15.830
instead of the fire.

00:02:17.500 --> 00:02:21.910
North Korea is unimaginable.

00:02:22.998 --> 00:02:25.207
It's very hard for me

00:02:25.231 --> 00:02:29.331
when people ask me
what it feels like to live there.

00:02:30.579 --> 00:02:32.686
To be honest,

00:02:32.710 --> 00:02:33.947
I tell you:

00:02:33.971 --> 00:02:36.424
you can't even imagine it.

00:02:39.070 --> 00:02:43.608
The words in any language can't describe,

00:02:43.632 --> 00:02:46.371
because it's a totally different planet,

00:02:47.458 --> 00:02:51.878
as you cannot imagine
your life on Mars right now.

00:02:53.122 --> 00:02:58.540
For example, the word "love"
has only one meaning:

00:02:59.393 --> 00:03:01.181
love for the Dear Leader.

00:03:03.511 --> 00:03:07.666
There's no concept
of romantic love in North Korea.

00:03:09.222 --> 00:03:12.234
And if you don't know the words,

00:03:12.258 --> 00:03:15.800
that means you don't
understand the concept,

00:03:17.578 --> 00:03:23.612
and therefore, you don't even realize
that concept is even a possibility.

00:03:25.422 --> 00:03:28.040
Let me give you another example.

00:03:29.096 --> 00:03:31.386
Growing up in North Korea,

00:03:31.410 --> 00:03:37.016
we truly believed that our Dear Leader
is an almighty god

00:03:37.040 --> 00:03:39.611
who can even read my thoughts.

00:03:40.350 --> 00:03:44.255
I was even afraid to think in North Korea.

00:03:45.619 --> 00:03:47.930
We are told that he's starving for us,

00:03:47.954 --> 00:03:50.252
and he's working tirelessly for us,

00:03:50.276 --> 00:03:52.709
and my heart just broke for him.

00:03:53.802 --> 00:03:56.577
When I escaped to South Korea,

00:03:56.601 --> 00:04:00.540
people told me that
he was actually a dictator,

00:04:00.564 --> 00:04:02.332
he had cars,

00:04:02.356 --> 00:04:03.927
many, many resorts,

00:04:03.951 --> 00:04:06.890
and he had an ultraluxurious life.

00:04:08.803 --> 00:04:12.901
And then I remember
looking at a picture of him,

00:04:12.925 --> 00:04:16.225
realizing for the first time

00:04:16.249 --> 00:04:19.897
that he is the largest guy in the picture.

00:04:19.921 --> 00:04:21.663
(Laughter)

00:04:22.334 --> 00:04:23.879
And it hit me.

00:04:23.903 --> 00:04:28.612
Finally, I realized he wasn't starving.

00:04:29.632 --> 00:04:32.800
But I was never able to see that before,

00:04:32.824 --> 00:04:36.539
until someone told me that he was fat.

00:04:36.563 --> 00:04:37.684
(Laughter)

00:04:37.708 --> 00:04:41.426
Really, someone had to teach me
that he was fat.

00:04:42.200 --> 00:04:46.314
If you have never practiced
critical thinking,

00:04:46.338 --> 00:04:50.051
then you simply see
what you're told to see.

00:04:52.395 --> 00:04:55.425
The biggest question also people ask me

00:04:55.449 --> 00:04:58.904
is: "Why is there no revolution
inside North Korea?

00:04:58.928 --> 00:05:00.210
Are we dumb?

00:05:01.202 --> 00:05:06.151
Why is there no revolution
for 70 years of this oppression?"

00:05:07.531 --> 00:05:08.829
And I say:

00:05:10.305 --> 00:05:12.177
If you don't know you're a slave,

00:05:13.050 --> 00:05:17.270
if you don't know
you're isolated or oppressed,

00:05:18.095 --> 00:05:20.080
how do you fight to be free?

00:05:22.676 --> 00:05:25.901
I mean, if you know you're isolated,

00:05:25.925 --> 00:05:28.083
that means you are not isolated.

00:05:28.955 --> 00:05:33.830
Not knowing is the true
definition of isolation,

00:05:33.854 --> 00:05:35.962
and that's why I never knew

00:05:35.986 --> 00:05:39.534
I was isolated when I was in North Korea.

00:05:39.558 --> 00:05:43.255
I literally thought I was
in the center of the universe.

00:05:45.517 --> 00:05:51.278
So here is my idea worth spreading:

00:05:52.622 --> 00:05:54.201
a lot of people think

00:05:54.225 --> 00:05:58.893
humans inherently know
what is right and wrong,

00:05:58.917 --> 00:06:02.491
the difference between
justice and injustice,

00:06:03.327 --> 00:06:06.411
what we deserve and we don't deserve.

00:06:07.647 --> 00:06:09.540
I tell them: BS.

00:06:10.140 --> 00:06:11.754
(Laughter)

00:06:11.778 --> 00:06:14.015
(Applause)

00:06:18.462 --> 00:06:19.770
Everything,

00:06:21.231 --> 00:06:22.999
everything must be taught,

00:06:24.197 --> 00:06:25.888
including compassion.

00:06:27.965 --> 00:06:34.187
If I see someone dying
on the street right now,

00:06:34.211 --> 00:06:37.051
I will do anything to save that person.

00:06:39.106 --> 00:06:41.006
But when I was in North Korea,

00:06:41.942 --> 00:06:46.283
I saw people dying
and dead on the streets.

00:06:47.219 --> 00:06:48.596
I felt nothing.

00:06:49.580 --> 00:06:51.489
Not because I'm a psychopath,

00:06:52.471 --> 00:06:56.277
but because I never learned
the concept of compassion.

00:06:57.082 --> 00:07:02.336
Only, I felt compassion,
empathy and sympathy in my heart

00:07:02.360 --> 00:07:05.934
after I learned the word
"compassion" and the concept,

00:07:05.958 --> 00:07:07.452
and I feel them now.

00:07:10.169 --> 00:07:16.614
Now I live in the United States
as a free person.

00:07:16.638 --> 00:07:17.773
(Applause)

00:07:17.797 --> 00:07:19.314
Thank you.

00:07:19.338 --> 00:07:23.256
(Applause)

00:07:24.113 --> 00:07:26.224
And recently,

00:07:26.248 --> 00:07:30.307
the leader of the free country,
our President Trump,

00:07:30.331 --> 00:07:33.485
met with my former god.

00:07:35.177 --> 00:07:39.894
And he decided human rights
is not important enough

00:07:39.918 --> 00:07:43.146
to include in his agendas,

00:07:43.170 --> 00:07:45.012
and he did not talk about it.

00:07:47.035 --> 00:07:49.817
And it scares me.

00:07:50.718 --> 00:07:53.994
We live in a world right now

00:07:54.018 --> 00:08:00.396
where a dictator can be praised
for executing his uncle,

00:08:00.420 --> 00:08:02.973
for killing his half brother,

00:08:02.997 --> 00:08:06.000
killing thousands of North Koreans.

00:08:06.024 --> 00:08:09.062
And that was worthy of praise.

00:08:10.829 --> 00:08:13.165
And also it made me think:

00:08:14.291 --> 00:08:20.865
perhaps we all need to be taught
something new about freedom now.

00:08:24.926 --> 00:08:27.822
Freedom is fragile.

00:08:29.140 --> 00:08:32.265
I don't want to alarm you, but it is.

00:08:33.426 --> 00:08:36.517
It only took three generations

00:08:36.541 --> 00:08:42.136
to make North Korea into
George Orwell's "1984."

00:08:42.965 --> 00:08:45.261
It took only three generations.

00:08:48.233 --> 00:08:52.746
If we don't fight for human rights

00:08:52.770 --> 00:08:56.850
for the people who are oppressed
right now who don't have a voice,

00:08:56.874 --> 00:08:58.707
as free people here,

00:09:00.000 --> 00:09:02.995
who will fight for us
when we are not free?

00:09:04.976 --> 00:09:09.119
Machines? Animals? I don't know.

00:09:11.889 --> 00:09:17.322
I think it's wonderful
that we care about climate change,

00:09:17.346 --> 00:09:19.899
animal rights, gender equality,

00:09:19.923 --> 00:09:21.650
all of these things.

00:09:21.674 --> 00:09:24.759
The fact that we care
about animals' rights,

00:09:24.783 --> 00:09:28.378
that means that's
how beautiful our heart is,

00:09:28.402 --> 00:09:32.273
that we care about someone
who cannot speak for themselves.

00:09:32.932 --> 00:09:38.344
And North Koreans right now
cannot speak for themselves.

00:09:38.900 --> 00:09:42.724
They don't have internet
in the 21st century.

00:09:42.748 --> 00:09:45.339
We don't have electricity,

00:09:45.363 --> 00:09:49.084
and it is the darkest place
on earth right now.

00:09:50.618 --> 00:09:54.403
Now I want to say something
to my fellow North Koreans

00:09:54.427 --> 00:09:56.632
who are living in that darkness.

00:09:58.050 --> 00:09:59.805
They might not believe this,

00:09:59.829 --> 00:10:04.681
but I want to tell them
that an alternative life is possible.

00:10:04.705 --> 00:10:06.043
Be free.

00:10:07.709 --> 00:10:11.459
From my experience,

00:10:11.483 --> 00:10:14.593
literally anything is possible.

00:10:16.264 --> 00:10:17.796
I was bought,

00:10:17.820 --> 00:10:20.188
I was sold as a slave.

00:10:20.212 --> 00:10:22.432
But now I'm here,

00:10:22.456 --> 00:10:25.656
and that is why I believe in miracles.

00:10:27.462 --> 00:10:30.667
The one thing that I learned from history

00:10:30.691 --> 00:10:35.705
is that nothing is forever in this world.

00:10:35.729 --> 00:10:41.151
And that is why we have
every reason to be hopeful.

00:10:41.175 --> 00:10:42.605
Thank you.

00:10:42.629 --> 00:10:46.904
(Applause)

